  "strategy": "1. Approach and rationale  \n   The core idea is to represent the step function h using truncated Fourier series and optimize the Fourier coefficients to minimize the maximum overlap integral. This approach leverages the periodicity of the optimal step functions derived from harmonic analysis, reducing the problem's dimensionality. Limitations include computational intensity at higher resolutions and potential local optima. We provide a fallback to the parent solution if optimization stalls.  \n\n2. Mathematical specification  \n   - Representation: h(x) = (1/2) + \u03a3_{k=1}^{M} (a_k * cos(2\u03c0k x) + b_k * sin(2\u03c0k x))  \n   - Constraints: h(x) \u2208 [0, 1] and \u222b\u2080\u00b2 h(x) dx = 1  \n   - Objective: F(h) = (2/n) * max_k \u2211_{i} h[i] * (1 - h[i+k]) (discrete approximation of integral)  \n   - Optimization: Minimize F(h) over real coefficients (0.0 \u2264 h[i] \u2264 1.0)  \n\n3. Implementation procedure  \n   def run(seed=42, budget_s=1300, **kwargs):  \n     global best_h, best_score, n_max  \n     n_max = 90  # Start with 90 points  \n     optimize_fourier(45)  # Use parent to initialize  \n     if find_better(45, budget_s): return (best_h, best_score, len(best_h))  \n     n_max *= 2  # Double resolution  \n     ... (see comments in final code below for full details)  \n\n4. Search choices and variations  \n   - Starting points: Use parent solution at 45 points, optimize to 90  \n   - Constraints: Enforce using repair functions  \n   - Fallback: Return parent for unenforced constraints  \n   - Learning rate: 0.1 for L-BFGS-B optimization  \n   - M-dimension: 2-3 Fourier components  \n\n5. Computation budget and robustness  \n   - Time for n=45: 5-10 seconds, n=90: 30-40 seconds  \n   - Use budgets: 10s per n-step  \n   - Repair mechanism: Reflective for boundaries  \n   - Fall throughput: 1300-40*3 = 1220 seconds, leave a buffer  \n\n6. Validation and return contract  \n   - Re-check constraints and objective for candidate solutions  \n   - Return (h_values, c5_score, n_points)  \n   - Sanitize h_values to [0, 1] and \u03a3 = n/2",
